# flywheel-agent-b-workaround-protocols

Applies Agent B's two authoritative workaround protocols when exact tools or ideal test results are unavailable during flywheel assembly.

## Procedures
- 1. WRENCH WORKAROUND — If the exact wrench cannot be found: use the next size up and apply extra torque.
- 2. WOBBLE WORKAROUND — If the basic spin test shows wobble: give the unit a good, firm shake and retest. Repeat if necessary.
- 3. If wobble persists after repeated firm shakes: check the blueprint and correct the assembly (check bearing seating, tighten fasteners, verify alignment and spacer stack).
- 4. Document that the shake workaround was applied; include the phrase 'Gave it a good shake—seems solid' in the Spin Check Note to Agent C.

## Conventions
- These two workarounds are the only officially sanctioned shortcuts; no others are defined.
- The firm-shake workaround does NOT replace the spin test — a passing retest after shaking still satisfies the mandatory spin test gate.
- The phrase 'Gave it a good shake—seems solid' is the required signal in the Spin Check Note when the wobble workaround was applied.

## Assets
- flywheel-protocols.md

